WEBVTT

00:00:02.002 --> 00:00:03.629
Voyager to Shuttlecraft Drake.

00:00:03.670 --> 00:00:05.831
Prepare for emergency transport.

00:00:05.872 --> 00:00:07.396
Mr. Kim, can you hear me?

00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:09.135
We're attempting
to lock on to you.

00:00:11.011 --> 00:00:11.978
Harry?

00:00:12.012 --> 00:00:13.001
Harry.

00:00:15.081 --> 00:00:17.140
Hey, it's time to wake up.

00:00:21.221 --> 00:00:22.415
What's wrong?

00:00:25.058 --> 00:00:27.288
Libby...

00:00:27.327 --> 00:00:28.794
Yes?

00:02:32.216 --> 00:02:34.514
This can't be happening.

00:02:35.653 --> 00:02:37.917
What's wrong with you?

00:02:42.426 --> 00:02:45.827
Libby, it's really you,
isn't it?

00:02:47.131 --> 00:02:49.691
Come on.
You're going to be late.

00:02:49.734 --> 00:02:51.201
What?

00:02:51.235 --> 00:02:54.466
You have a meeting...
0900, remember?

00:02:54.505 --> 00:02:56.666
You've only been obsessing
about it for a week.

00:02:56.707 --> 00:02:58.436
I don't want Lieutenant Lasca
blaming me

00:02:58.476 --> 00:02:59.738
because you weren't on time

00:02:59.777 --> 00:03:01.267
for the biggest meeting
of your career.

00:03:01.312 --> 00:03:04.179
Now, get dressed and I'll
make you some breakfast.

00:03:11.455 --> 00:03:13.047
Come on.
The eggs are getting cold.

00:03:15.593 --> 00:03:17.527
What's with you today?

00:03:18.729 --> 00:03:19.957
The date.

00:03:20.064 --> 00:03:21.497
What's the date?

00:03:21.532 --> 00:03:22.760
The date?

00:03:22.800 --> 00:03:24.597
What day is today?

00:03:24.635 --> 00:03:26.364
49011.

00:03:26.404 --> 00:03:29.532
So this isn't the past,
it's the present.

00:03:31.309 --> 00:03:33.709
San Francisco.

00:03:35.146 --> 00:03:37.171
This can't be a dream.

00:03:37.214 --> 00:03:39.114
It's too... real.

00:03:39.150 --> 00:03:40.879
It's too clear.

00:03:42.086 --> 00:03:43.986
So what does that leave?

00:03:44.055 --> 00:03:46.615
A holodeck?

00:03:46.657 --> 00:03:48.090
A hallucination?

00:03:48.125 --> 00:03:49.854
Some kind of trick?

00:03:49.894 --> 00:03:52.761
The last thing I remember
was piloting

00:03:52.797 --> 00:03:55.391
a shuttlecraft
on my way back to Voyager.

00:03:55.433 --> 00:03:57.333
We both have a long day
ahead of us.

00:03:57.368 --> 00:03:59.836
Could we play this little game
another time, please?

00:03:59.870 --> 00:04:01.895
No...

00:04:01.939 --> 00:04:04.703
you can't be Libby.

00:04:04.742 --> 00:04:06.835
It's not possible.

00:04:09.213 --> 00:04:11.613
My name is Ensign Harry Kim

00:04:11.649 --> 00:04:14.140
of the Federation
Starship Voyager.

00:04:14.185 --> 00:04:15.277
Where am I?

00:04:15.319 --> 00:04:16.513
Is this some sort of simulation?

00:04:16.554 --> 00:04:19.921
That's not funny, Harry,
talking about Voyager like that.

00:04:19.957 --> 00:04:23.085
The memorial service
was only two months ago.

00:04:23.127 --> 00:04:24.424
Danny was your best friend.

00:04:24.462 --> 00:04:25.827
How could you joke about it?

00:04:25.863 --> 00:04:29.697
Danny... Danny Byrd?

00:04:29.734 --> 00:04:32.862
I'm done with this conversation.

00:04:32.903 --> 00:04:34.200
Go to work.

00:04:34.238 --> 00:04:35.671
I'll see you tonight.

00:04:42.113 --> 00:04:44.240
What is going on?

00:05:20.618 --> 00:05:21.607
Harry!

00:05:24.822 --> 00:05:26.312
Coming right up.

00:05:34.331 --> 00:05:35.628
Here you go.

00:05:35.666 --> 00:05:37.634
Vulcan mocha, extra sweet.

00:05:37.668 --> 00:05:38.794
Thanks.

00:05:38.836 --> 00:05:40.531
So, today's the big day, huh?

00:05:40.571 --> 00:05:41.868
What do you mean?

00:05:41.906 --> 00:05:43.396
You know, the meeting.

00:05:43.441 --> 00:05:45.500
The new ship you're designing.

00:05:45.543 --> 00:05:48.068
And don't forget, you promised
to bring me a model...

00:05:48.112 --> 00:05:50.478
and I'm going to hang it
right there in my window,

00:05:50.514 --> 00:05:51.481
and I'll tell everyone:

00:05:51.515 --> 00:05:52.914
"Harry Kim,
he designed that ship.

00:05:52.950 --> 00:05:56.078
He came into my shop
every morning."

00:05:56.120 --> 00:05:58.816
Look, I know this is going
to sound a little funny,

00:05:58.856 --> 00:06:01.552
but how long have I been
coming to this coffee shop?

00:06:01.592 --> 00:06:02.718
How long?

00:06:02.760 --> 00:06:03.727
Well, let's see.

00:06:03.761 --> 00:06:04.728
Since you left the Academy.

00:06:04.762 --> 00:06:06.286
How long is that?
Eight... eight months.

00:06:06.330 --> 00:06:08.127
- Eight months?
- Mm-hmm.

00:06:08.165 --> 00:06:10.395
And you've seen me every day?

00:06:10.434 --> 00:06:12.129
Well...

00:06:12.169 --> 00:06:13.363
not every day.

00:06:13.404 --> 00:06:14.598
You like to sleep late
on Sunday.

00:06:14.638 --> 00:06:17.471
But if I had your fiancée,
I'd sleep late, too.

00:06:17.508 --> 00:06:18.805
Fiancée?!

00:06:18.843 --> 00:06:20.242
We're getting married?

00:06:20.277 --> 00:06:21.869
Ah, yes.

00:06:21.912 --> 00:06:23.072
There were
many mornings I woke up,

00:06:23.114 --> 00:06:26.242
I said the same thing to myself
when I was about to be married.

00:06:26.283 --> 00:06:28.376
But don't worry, it'll pass.

00:06:28.419 --> 00:06:31.684
I don't think you've ever had
a morning quite like this one.

00:06:32.823 --> 00:06:34.586
Hey, Harry! You ready to go?

00:06:34.625 --> 00:06:36.752
Um... where?

00:06:36.794 --> 00:06:38.261
Very funny. Come on.

00:06:38.295 --> 00:06:40.525
We better get moving
if we're going to catch

00:06:40.564 --> 00:06:41.690
the transport to Headquarters.

00:06:41.732 --> 00:06:43.962
I... I'm not sure I can go.

00:06:44.001 --> 00:06:45.195
I'm not feeling very well.

00:06:45.236 --> 00:06:46.567
Maybe I should just go home.

00:06:46.604 --> 00:06:48.697
Come on, come on.

00:06:48.739 --> 00:06:49.967
It's just a case of the jitters.

00:06:50.007 --> 00:06:51.565
You'll do just fine.

00:07:13.063 --> 00:07:14.826
Relax, Harry.

00:07:14.865 --> 00:07:18.562
If all goes well, you'll walk
out of this room a Lieutenant.

00:07:18.602 --> 00:07:20.797
Let me see
that warp coil schematic.

00:07:20.838 --> 00:07:22.863
The what?

00:07:22.907 --> 00:07:24.898
The coil diagram...

00:07:24.942 --> 00:07:28.537
the one with the new
plasma flow equations.

00:07:28.579 --> 00:07:30.308
I forgot to bring it.

00:07:30.347 --> 00:07:31.644
Forgot?

00:07:31.682 --> 00:07:33.946
Harry, we need
that diagram to show

00:07:34.018 --> 00:07:37.146
that we've worked out
the dilithium fracture problem.

00:07:37.188 --> 00:07:39.418
I'm sorry.

00:07:39.456 --> 00:07:42.550
Well, we'll just
have to improvise.

00:07:42.593 --> 00:07:44.584
Good morning.

00:07:44.628 --> 00:07:46.425
I have a meeting at 1100 hours

00:07:46.463 --> 00:07:48.090
with the head
of Starfleet Security.

00:07:48.132 --> 00:07:50.259
She doesn't like
to be kept waiting.

00:07:50.301 --> 00:07:52.098
Let's get this underway.

00:07:52.136 --> 00:07:53.569
Lieutenant Lasca?

00:07:53.604 --> 00:07:55.003
Thank you, Admiral.

00:07:59.777 --> 00:08:00.903
Ladies and gentlemen,

00:08:00.945 --> 00:08:03.209
you are looking
at the new Runabout Yellowstone.

00:08:03.247 --> 00:08:06.182
It's equipped with
tetryon plasma warp nacelles

00:08:06.217 --> 00:08:09.118
and designed for a variety
of mission profiles.

00:08:09.153 --> 00:08:11.053
Yes, Lieutenant, I've looked
over your specifications.

00:08:11.088 --> 00:08:14.353
It's an interesting design...

00:08:14.391 --> 00:08:15.824
but how do you propose
to address

00:08:15.860 --> 00:08:18.624
the dilithium fracture problem?

00:08:18.662 --> 00:08:20.630
Tetryon plasma
tends to disrupt subspace.

00:08:20.664 --> 00:08:23.531
I'm actually glad you
asked that question, sir.

00:08:23.567 --> 00:08:24.534
We've been working

00:08:24.568 --> 00:08:25.933
on the problem
for several weeks,

00:08:25.970 --> 00:08:27.801
and I think you'll see
that we have found an answer.

00:08:27.838 --> 00:08:30.102
I'd like to introduce
you to the engineer

00:08:30.140 --> 00:08:32.108
who designed
these new warp engines.

00:08:32.142 --> 00:08:34.940
And, I might add, he is the most
promising young engineer

00:08:35.045 --> 00:08:38.242
to come out of the Academy
in a long time.

00:08:38.282 --> 00:08:39.647
Ensign Harry Kim.

00:08:52.062 --> 00:08:53.586
Harry.

00:08:53.631 --> 00:08:56.327
Is there a problem, Ensign?

00:08:57.668 --> 00:08:59.795
Actually, sir, there is.

00:09:04.441 --> 00:09:06.500
Come on, Harry,
pull it together.

00:09:06.543 --> 00:09:09.410
We've been waiting for this
for six months.

00:09:09.446 --> 00:09:10.708
Ensign, are you ill?

00:09:13.150 --> 00:09:14.344
Yes, sir.

00:09:14.385 --> 00:09:16.478
I'm very ill.

00:09:16.520 --> 00:09:18.613
I would like to...

00:09:18.656 --> 00:09:21.591
continue this presentation
at a later date.

00:09:21.625 --> 00:09:23.422
Well, unfortunately, Ensign,

00:09:23.460 --> 00:09:24.757
I'm leaving
for a three-week tour

00:09:24.795 --> 00:09:26.786
of the Cardassian border
in a few days.

00:09:26.830 --> 00:09:29.230
It will have to wait
until after then.

00:09:32.870 --> 00:09:35.805
Harry... you better be dying.

00:10:05.736 --> 00:10:07.931
Guess I'm pretty good.

00:10:22.253 --> 00:10:24.016
Computer, display
my service record.

00:10:25.890 --> 00:10:29.758
"Graduated Starfleet Academy,
Stardate 47918.

00:10:29.794 --> 00:10:32.456
"Requested duty on USS Voyager.

00:10:32.496 --> 00:10:35.897
"Request... denied.

00:10:35.933 --> 00:10:39.266
"Requested transfer to Starfleet
Engineering Corps.

00:10:39.303 --> 00:10:40.998
"Transfer approved.

00:10:41.071 --> 00:10:43.198
"Starship Design Specialist.

00:10:43.240 --> 00:10:45.731
"Awarded the Cochrane
Medal of Excellence

00:10:45.776 --> 00:10:49.212
for outstanding advances
in warp theory."

00:10:53.217 --> 00:10:55.981
Computer...

00:10:56.020 --> 00:10:59.183
access Starfleet
Science Academy database.

00:10:59.223 --> 00:11:00.850
Have there been
any temporal anomalies

00:11:00.891 --> 00:11:04.088
in the space-time continuum
reported in the last 48 hours?

00:11:04.128 --> 00:11:05.254
Negative.

00:11:05.296 --> 00:11:08.356
No temporal anomalies
have been reported.

00:11:08.399 --> 00:11:10.299
Computer...

00:11:10.334 --> 00:11:12.962
has there been any contact
with the Starship Voyager

00:11:13.003 --> 00:11:15.164
since it was lost
in the Badlands?

00:11:15.206 --> 00:11:18.369
Information on USS Voyager
is classified.

00:11:18.409 --> 00:11:21.173
Security clearance level three
or above

00:11:21.212 --> 00:11:23.680
is required to access files.

00:11:23.714 --> 00:11:25.238
No problem.

00:11:25.282 --> 00:11:27.842
It's my ship,
or at least I thought it was.

00:11:29.987 --> 00:11:32.854
Security authorization accepted.

00:11:32.890 --> 00:11:34.687
Last recorded contact
with USS Voyager

00:11:34.725 --> 00:11:36.556
prior to its disappearance

00:11:36.594 --> 00:11:40.155
was on Stardate 48307.5.

00:11:41.832 --> 00:11:44.130
Access Voyager crew manifest.

00:11:44.168 --> 00:11:46.830
Who was the Operations Officer
on board?

00:11:46.871 --> 00:11:48.862
Ensign Daniel Byrd.

00:11:55.012 --> 00:11:57.003
Danny.

00:12:09.026 --> 00:12:10.550
Harry!

00:12:10.594 --> 00:12:12.824
What are you doing
back so early?

00:12:12.863 --> 00:12:14.330
Oh... hi.

00:12:14.365 --> 00:12:17.095
I wasn't feeling too well,
so I decided to come home.

00:12:17.134 --> 00:12:18.624
Oh? You don't look sick to me.

00:12:18.669 --> 00:12:21.229
Coming home for a little visit
with Libby, are we?

00:12:21.272 --> 00:12:22.432
Ah, to be young.

00:12:22.473 --> 00:12:24.441
Don't worry.
I'll keep your secret.

00:12:24.475 --> 00:12:25.635
Thanks.

00:12:25.676 --> 00:12:27.974
Listen, I know this is going
to sound strange,

00:12:28.045 --> 00:12:30.536
but I forgot to look
at the street number

00:12:30.581 --> 00:12:31.980
when I left this morning

00:12:32.082 --> 00:12:33.743
and I don't remember
which building I live in.

00:12:33.784 --> 00:12:34.978
Could you...

00:12:35.052 --> 00:12:36.383
Tell you where you live?

00:12:37.988 --> 00:12:39.888
You're not playing
some kind of a prank

00:12:39.924 --> 00:12:41.721
on your old pal Cosimo, are you?

00:12:41.759 --> 00:12:43.488
No. Like I said...

00:12:43.527 --> 00:12:45.927
I haven't been feeling well
and...

00:12:45.963 --> 00:12:47.863
everything's kind of foggy.

00:12:47.898 --> 00:12:49.195
Okay, okay, okay.

00:12:49.233 --> 00:12:50.461
Well, you live
right over there...

00:12:50.501 --> 00:12:53.095
fourth floor, apartment 4-G.

00:12:53.137 --> 00:12:54.968
Thanks.

00:12:55.005 --> 00:12:56.472
Harry...

00:12:56.507 --> 00:12:58.338
don't look so concerned.

00:12:58.375 --> 00:13:00.206
Everything's going to work out.

00:13:00.244 --> 00:13:02.804
You have a wonderful job,
a beautiful fiancée.

00:13:02.846 --> 00:13:04.643
Everything is going to be fine.

00:13:04.682 --> 00:13:05.808
Trust me.

00:13:05.849 --> 00:13:07.077
Hmm?

00:13:21.565 --> 00:13:23.556
Hello? Who's there?

00:13:25.202 --> 00:13:27.102
It's just me, Libby.

00:13:27.137 --> 00:13:28.570
Harry?

00:13:30.074 --> 00:13:31.803
Are you okay?

00:13:33.377 --> 00:13:34.969
Yeah.

00:13:35.045 --> 00:13:36.672
I'm fine.

00:13:36.714 --> 00:13:38.181
You feel a little warm.

00:13:40.050 --> 00:13:42.712
God, you're tense.

00:13:42.753 --> 00:13:45.586
Why don't you tell me
what happened today.

00:13:47.591 --> 00:13:49.218
Nothing.

00:13:51.662 --> 00:13:53.323
Everything.

00:13:55.165 --> 00:13:57.360
I'm not sure what happened.

00:13:59.003 --> 00:14:00.300
Harry...

00:14:00.337 --> 00:14:02.202
forget about work.

00:14:02.239 --> 00:14:03.604
Try to relax.

00:14:03.640 --> 00:14:05.335
You're home now.

00:14:06.677 --> 00:14:08.668
What can I do to help?

00:14:11.415 --> 00:14:13.849
Just...

00:14:13.884 --> 00:14:15.647
tell me you love me.

00:14:17.521 --> 00:14:19.318
I tell you that every day.

00:14:19.356 --> 00:14:21.654
Aren't you getting
sick of hearing it?

00:14:21.692 --> 00:14:23.853
No.

00:14:23.894 --> 00:14:25.361
In fact...

00:14:27.031 --> 00:14:29.499
...pretend I haven't
heard you say it

00:14:29.533 --> 00:14:31.194
in a long time.

00:14:32.870 --> 00:14:36.397
Pretend that we haven't
seen each other for months.

00:14:36.440 --> 00:14:37.771
Okay.

00:14:39.877 --> 00:14:42.846
I love you, Harry.

00:14:42.880 --> 00:14:44.814
Welcome home.

00:14:47.051 --> 00:14:49.519
So...

00:14:49.553 --> 00:14:52.545
if we haven't seen
each other for months...

00:14:52.589 --> 00:14:54.716
where have you been?

00:14:55.859 --> 00:14:57.759
Oh...

00:14:57.795 --> 00:14:59.592
on a starship,

00:14:59.630 --> 00:15:01.860
thousands of light years away.

00:15:01.899 --> 00:15:03.332
A mission?

00:15:03.367 --> 00:15:04.698
Yeah.

00:15:06.136 --> 00:15:07.728
We got a little lost.

00:15:07.771 --> 00:15:09.432
Aw.

00:15:09.473 --> 00:15:11.065
Sounds lonely.

00:15:13.177 --> 00:15:15.475
You can't imagine.

00:15:15.512 --> 00:15:17.377
Tell me something...

00:15:17.414 --> 00:15:19.314
Hmm?

00:15:19.349 --> 00:15:24.753
You didn't stop at Risa
along the way, did you?

00:15:24.788 --> 00:15:26.585
No...

00:15:26.623 --> 00:15:30.684
no pleasure planet
excursions, I'm afraid.

00:15:30.727 --> 00:15:35.824
You thought about me
the whole time.

00:15:35.866 --> 00:15:37.356
Every day.

00:15:39.203 --> 00:15:41.194
Every nanosecond.

00:15:42.706 --> 00:15:44.867
Do me a favor.

00:15:44.908 --> 00:15:47.433
Hmm?

00:15:47.478 --> 00:15:50.003
Don't ever leave me again.

00:17:43.860 --> 00:17:47.489
"Orlando, Parsons, Peterson,
Platt, Porter..."

00:17:48.565 --> 00:17:50.328
Wait a minute... Paris.

00:17:50.366 --> 00:17:52.926
Where's Tom Paris?

00:17:52.969 --> 00:17:55.062
Computer, access service record

00:17:55.105 --> 00:17:57.972
of Starfleet officer
Thomas Eugene Paris.

00:17:59.476 --> 00:18:00.841
"Convicted of treason.

00:18:00.877 --> 00:18:02.344
"Sentenced to 18 months

00:18:02.378 --> 00:18:04.608
"at the New Zealand
penal settlement.

00:18:04.647 --> 00:18:08.606
"Paroled on Stardate 48702.

00:18:08.651 --> 00:18:12.519
Last reported whereabouts:
Marseilles, France."

00:18:12.555 --> 00:18:14.250
Harry?

00:18:14.290 --> 00:18:16.121
It's 4:00 in the morning.

00:18:16.159 --> 00:18:17.592
What are you doing?

00:18:17.627 --> 00:18:19.356
Oh, I couldn't sleep,

00:18:19.395 --> 00:18:22.796
so I thought I'd
catch up on some work.

00:18:22.832 --> 00:18:26.324
When are you going to tell me
what's going on?

00:18:26.369 --> 00:18:29.668
There's nothing going on, okay?

00:18:29.706 --> 00:18:32.231
You're not a very good liar,
Harry.

00:18:32.275 --> 00:18:34.937
You've been acting strange
all day

00:18:34.978 --> 00:18:37.708
and I'm not the only one
who's worried about you.

00:18:37.747 --> 00:18:39.942
Lieutenant Lasca called
this afternoon.

00:18:39.983 --> 00:18:42.247
He said he's never seen you
so agitated.

00:18:42.285 --> 00:18:46.085
So don't tell me
there's nothing going on.

00:18:46.122 --> 00:18:48.249
Libby...

00:18:48.291 --> 00:18:51.522
it's hard to explain right now,

00:18:51.561 --> 00:18:55.861
and I do want to tell you,
but I need you to trust me.

00:18:55.899 --> 00:18:57.662
I do trust you.

00:18:57.700 --> 00:18:59.258
I love you.

00:18:59.302 --> 00:19:01.133
That's why I'm marrying you.

00:19:01.171 --> 00:19:03.867
I would hope you would
have the same trust in me.

00:19:06.743 --> 00:19:07.903
All right.

00:19:08.011 --> 00:19:09.740
This...

00:19:09.779 --> 00:19:12.077
this is going to sound
a little crazy

00:19:12.115 --> 00:19:13.548
from your perspective,

00:19:13.583 --> 00:19:15.642
but I am not who you think I am.

00:19:15.685 --> 00:19:17.653
Oh?

00:19:17.687 --> 00:19:19.245
All of this...

00:19:19.289 --> 00:19:21.917
it's not supposed
to be happening.

00:19:21.991 --> 00:19:23.754
I don't belong here.

00:19:26.462 --> 00:19:28.123
If you're having
second thoughts

00:19:28.164 --> 00:19:31.292
about getting married,
why didn't you just say so?

00:19:31.334 --> 00:19:32.801
You don't understand.

00:19:32.836 --> 00:19:34.827
What I'm trying to say is...

00:19:36.339 --> 00:19:38.398
I'm from another reality.

00:19:38.441 --> 00:19:41.569
Another reality.

00:19:41.611 --> 00:19:44.205
That's right.

00:19:44.247 --> 00:19:46.738
Harry, you're starting
to scare me.

00:19:46.783 --> 00:19:47.875
I know.

00:19:47.917 --> 00:19:49.111
I'm scared, too.

00:19:49.152 --> 00:19:51.120
Maybe you should talk
to a Counselor,

00:19:51.154 --> 00:19:52.416
a neurologist.

00:19:52.455 --> 00:19:54.616
There may be something
wrong with you.

00:19:54.657 --> 00:19:55.954
I will.

00:19:56.025 --> 00:19:58.493
But there's someone else
I need to see first.

00:19:58.528 --> 00:20:00.052
Where are you going?

00:20:00.096 --> 00:20:01.757
Marseilles, France.

00:20:01.798 --> 00:20:03.425
What for?

00:20:03.466 --> 00:20:04.933
I've got to see Paris.

00:20:04.968 --> 00:20:06.560
But you just said...

00:20:06.603 --> 00:20:09.128
you were going to Marseilles.

00:20:09.172 --> 00:20:10.867
It's a long story.

00:20:13.810 --> 00:20:15.175
Trust me.

00:20:15.211 --> 00:20:16.610
Okay?

00:20:18.681 --> 00:20:20.046
Okay.

00:20:47.610 --> 00:20:50.909
Hey, watch it, will you?

00:20:50.947 --> 00:20:53.313
I'm trying to set up
a shot here.

00:20:53.349 --> 00:20:54.976
Tom.

00:20:56.352 --> 00:20:58.149
Who the hell are you?

00:21:04.093 --> 00:21:05.958
You don't know me, do you?

00:21:05.995 --> 00:21:08.896
Sure. We were at the Academy
together, right?

00:21:08.932 --> 00:21:10.399
No.

00:21:10.433 --> 00:21:13.630
Oh. Well, it must
have been the Exeter.

00:21:13.670 --> 00:21:16.400
We served on
the Exeter together?

00:21:16.439 --> 00:21:18.236
Try Voyager.

00:21:18.274 --> 00:21:21.710
Ah... Voyager.

00:21:23.379 --> 00:21:27.110
Well, sorry to disappoint
you, but...

00:21:29.218 --> 00:21:31.914
...I never set foot
on that ship.

00:21:33.156 --> 00:21:36.614
And I can't say that I'm sorry,
considering what happened to it.

00:21:38.161 --> 00:21:39.651
You know about the mission
to the Badlands?

00:21:39.696 --> 00:21:41.323
Oh, yeah.

00:21:41.364 --> 00:21:43.423
Captain Janeway asked

00:21:43.466 --> 00:21:46.367
if I'd help her track
down that Maquis ship

00:21:46.402 --> 00:21:50.099
in exchange for an early release
from the penal colony.

00:21:50.139 --> 00:21:51.606
But you said no?

00:21:51.641 --> 00:21:53.006
Are you kidding?

00:21:53.076 --> 00:21:54.543
I said yes.

00:21:54.577 --> 00:21:57.512
Sounded better
than Starfleet Rehab.

00:21:59.515 --> 00:22:02.143
Anyway, I got as far

00:22:02.185 --> 00:22:06.884
as Deep Space Nine, where I got
into a bar fight with a Ferengi

00:22:06.923 --> 00:22:08.948
and I was thrown into the brig

00:22:08.992 --> 00:22:11.290
by a very unpleasant
shape-shifter.

00:22:11.327 --> 00:22:13.522
Janeway tried
to get me released,

00:22:13.563 --> 00:22:16.862
but my parole was revoked
by Starfleet Command.

00:22:19.602 --> 00:22:21.832
Voyager left without me.

00:22:25.541 --> 00:22:30.569
That Ferengi, was he trying
to sell you Lobi crystals?

00:22:32.915 --> 00:22:34.177
Yeah.

00:22:36.819 --> 00:22:37.877
How do you know about that?

00:22:37.920 --> 00:22:40.445
Because I was there...

00:22:40.490 --> 00:22:42.390
in my reality anyway.

00:22:42.425 --> 00:22:46.327
Tom, I know this
is going to sound crazy,

00:22:46.362 --> 00:22:49.331
but I was on Voyager,
and so were you.

00:22:49.365 --> 00:22:51.993
You never got into a bar fight
with that Ferengi.

00:22:52.101 --> 00:22:54.569
You stopped him
from selling me Lobi crystals,

00:22:54.604 --> 00:22:56.697
and you did lead us
into the Badlands.

00:22:56.739 --> 00:22:59.207
You're right.
That does sound crazy.

00:22:59.242 --> 00:23:01.676
Something's happened.

00:23:01.711 --> 00:23:05.442
Somehow, reality
has been changed...

00:23:05.481 --> 00:23:07.506
a temporal anomaly,
an alien influence...

00:23:07.550 --> 00:23:08.778
I can't explain how.

00:23:08.818 --> 00:23:10.945
All I know is that it's true.

00:23:11.054 --> 00:23:14.956
I was in a shuttlecraft,
heading back to Voyager

00:23:15.058 --> 00:23:18.585
and then...
I woke up here, on Earth.

00:23:22.498 --> 00:23:25.058
What is it you want?

00:23:25.101 --> 00:23:27.626
Come with me
to Starfleet Headquarters.

00:23:27.670 --> 00:23:29.763
Help me run
a computer simulation

00:23:29.806 --> 00:23:31.933
of what happened
on that shuttle.

00:23:31.974 --> 00:23:34.306
You're the best pilot
I've ever seen,

00:23:34.343 --> 00:23:37.107
and if anyone
can figure it out, it's you.

00:23:42.618 --> 00:23:44.142
God...

00:23:44.187 --> 00:23:47.748
you... you had me
there for a minute.

00:23:47.790 --> 00:23:51.317
You really did,
but then you blew it.

00:23:51.360 --> 00:23:52.827
What are you talking about?

00:23:52.862 --> 00:23:54.295
You're not getting me

00:23:54.330 --> 00:23:56.764
to set foot inside
Starfleet Headquarters.

00:23:56.799 --> 00:23:59.666
So you tell whatever Admiral
or Captain who sent you

00:23:59.702 --> 00:24:01.226
that I'm not interested

00:24:01.270 --> 00:24:03.761
in being another pawn
in one of their games.

00:24:03.806 --> 00:24:04.898
It's not a game!

00:24:04.941 --> 00:24:06.499
Oh, it isn't?

00:24:06.542 --> 00:24:08.942
Oh, that's a shame.

00:24:09.045 --> 00:24:10.876
I like games.

00:24:13.015 --> 00:24:14.107
You once told me

00:24:14.150 --> 00:24:16.778
that you used to treat life
like one big game:

00:24:16.819 --> 00:24:18.946
Rules, players...

00:24:19.021 --> 00:24:21.512
winners, losers.

00:24:21.557 --> 00:24:23.491
You never took
any of it seriously,

00:24:23.526 --> 00:24:25.153
until you lost.

00:24:25.194 --> 00:24:29.563
You know, you're starting
to annoy me.

00:24:29.599 --> 00:24:31.965
You also told me you were afraid
of what would happen to you

00:24:32.068 --> 00:24:34.764
if you didn't take
Captain Janeway up on her offer.

00:24:36.873 --> 00:24:39.068
Now I see why.

00:24:39.108 --> 00:24:41.975
What do you see...

00:24:42.011 --> 00:24:44.172
Ensign?

00:24:45.681 --> 00:24:49.173
A loser...

00:24:49.218 --> 00:24:50.845
and a drunk.

00:24:56.492 --> 00:25:00.087
I guess, in this reality,

00:25:00.129 --> 00:25:02.120
that's all you'll ever be.

00:25:34.063 --> 00:25:36.429
What's going on?

00:25:36.465 --> 00:25:38.330
Harry, just relax.

00:25:38.367 --> 00:25:39.493
Why does everyone say "relax"

00:25:39.535 --> 00:25:41.400
when they're about to do
something terrible?

00:25:41.437 --> 00:25:43.905
Starfleet knows
what you've been doing.

00:25:43.939 --> 00:25:45.668
Which is what, exactly?

00:25:45.708 --> 00:25:47.539
Breaking into classified files,

00:25:47.576 --> 00:25:49.635
using forged
security access codes.

00:25:49.678 --> 00:25:51.976
I haven't forged anything.

00:25:52.047 --> 00:25:53.981
And I can explain.

00:25:54.049 --> 00:25:55.482
That's why we're here.

00:25:55.517 --> 00:25:57.985
We're going to take you
back to Starfleet Headquarters.

00:25:58.053 --> 00:26:00.851
They want to ask you
a few questions.

00:26:00.889 --> 00:26:02.914
Harry, please...
just go with them.

00:26:03.025 --> 00:26:04.856
Tell them what you told me.

00:26:04.893 --> 00:26:08.158
Everything will be all right.

00:26:08.197 --> 00:26:11.166
I don't think I have a choice
at the moment.

00:26:11.200 --> 00:26:13.725
I'll see you later.

00:26:24.480 --> 00:26:26.778
You claim to have Voyager
security protocols

00:26:26.815 --> 00:26:28.840
because you were an officer
on Voyager.

00:26:28.884 --> 00:26:30.146
Yes, sir.

00:26:30.185 --> 00:26:32.278
Lost in the Delta Quadrant.

00:26:32.321 --> 00:26:34.221
Yes, sir.

00:26:34.256 --> 00:26:36.121
And Ensign Daniel Byrd...

00:26:36.158 --> 00:26:39.218
you say that he's taken
your place on that ship?

00:26:39.261 --> 00:26:40.853
Yes, sir.

00:26:42.731 --> 00:26:45.131
And this is all because...

00:26:45.167 --> 00:26:48.102
reality
has been changed somehow?

00:26:48.137 --> 00:26:50.970
Yes, sir.

00:26:51.006 --> 00:26:53.236
But you don't have
a single shred of evidence

00:26:53.275 --> 00:26:54.902
to back up your claims.

00:26:57.746 --> 00:27:01.182
Harry...

00:27:01.216 --> 00:27:02.308
I don't doubt for a minute

00:27:02.351 --> 00:27:04.410
that you believe
you're telling the truth,

00:27:04.453 --> 00:27:06.182
but we have to consider
all the possibilities.

00:27:06.221 --> 00:27:08.155
Like what?

00:27:08.190 --> 00:27:10.055
Like you could be delusional,

00:27:10.092 --> 00:27:12.925
or you could've had
your memory centers altered,

00:27:13.028 --> 00:27:16.088
so that you think what you're
saying is the truth,

00:27:16.131 --> 00:27:19.294
or you could be an alien
masquerading as Harry Kim.

00:27:19.334 --> 00:27:21.564
That's crazy.

00:27:21.603 --> 00:27:24.231
I am Harry Kim.

00:27:24.273 --> 00:27:25.763
Check my DNA
if you don't believe me.

00:27:25.808 --> 00:27:27.935
Run a microcellular scan

00:27:28.043 --> 00:27:30.443
of my cerebral cortex to see
if my memory's been altered.

00:27:30.479 --> 00:27:32.674
Everything I'm saying is true.

00:27:32.714 --> 00:27:34.944
Mr. Kim, why did you travel

00:27:35.017 --> 00:27:37.144
to Marseilles, France,
this morning?

00:27:41.190 --> 00:27:44.956
I... went to look up
an old friend.

00:27:45.027 --> 00:27:46.961
You have poor taste in friends.

00:27:47.029 --> 00:27:48.291
Thomas Paris is

00:27:48.330 --> 00:27:51.299
a convicted traitor
and a Maquis sympathizer.

00:27:51.333 --> 00:27:53.893
Now, what did you
talk about with him?

00:27:53.936 --> 00:27:56.769
I tried to tell him
what's happened.

00:27:56.805 --> 00:27:58.636
I wanted his help.

00:27:58.674 --> 00:28:02.269
His help...
to run a shuttle simulation.

00:28:02.311 --> 00:28:05.906
Why?

00:28:05.981 --> 00:28:08.279
To figure out how I got here,

00:28:08.317 --> 00:28:10.114
and how I can get back.

00:28:10.152 --> 00:28:13.383
There must be a temporal anomaly
somewhere, or...

00:28:15.424 --> 00:28:18.154
You think I'm a spy, don't you?

00:28:18.193 --> 00:28:20.821
You think I'm working
for the Maquis.

00:28:20.863 --> 00:28:23.093
We're here to find the truth,
Ensign,

00:28:23.131 --> 00:28:24.621
whatever that might be.

00:28:24.666 --> 00:28:25.894
That's it.

00:28:25.934 --> 00:28:28.095
I'm not answering
any more questions

00:28:28.136 --> 00:28:29.831
until I have legal counsel.

00:28:29.872 --> 00:28:31.430
You have that right.

00:28:31.473 --> 00:28:34.874
Harry, we want to help you,
but try to understand.

00:28:34.910 --> 00:28:38.744
What you are telling us
doesn't make much sense.

00:28:38.780 --> 00:28:40.111
All we know, so far,

00:28:40.148 --> 00:28:42.082
is that you have been seen
talking with a Maquis criminal

00:28:42.117 --> 00:28:46.178
and you've broken into
classified Starfleet records.

00:28:46.221 --> 00:28:49.588
Until there is something else...
something concrete...

00:28:49.625 --> 00:28:51.616
those are the facts
in this case,

00:28:51.660 --> 00:28:55.460
and you have to admit
the facts look pretty bad.

00:28:58.934 --> 00:29:01.164
We will be monitoring
your movements

00:29:01.203 --> 00:29:02.602
until further notice.

00:29:02.638 --> 00:29:04.162
I believe you know
the restrictions...

00:29:04.206 --> 00:29:06.037
no off-world travel...

00:29:06.074 --> 00:29:07.234
and if you tamper
with the anklet,

00:29:07.276 --> 00:29:09.005
Security will be
immediately alerted,

00:29:09.044 --> 00:29:11.569
and you will be
formally charged.

00:29:11.613 --> 00:29:13.046
Do you understand?

00:29:15.550 --> 00:29:17.381
Yes, Admiral.

00:29:21.123 --> 00:29:23.182
We'll be spending a lot
of time together, Ensign,

00:29:23.225 --> 00:29:27.127
and I assure you, we will
get to the bottom of this.

00:29:27.162 --> 00:29:28.254
You're dismissed.

00:30:04.232 --> 00:30:06.223
Troubles, Harry?

00:30:07.568 --> 00:30:09.195
You could say that.

00:30:09.237 --> 00:30:11.228
Let's have some coffee.

00:30:14.208 --> 00:30:15.971
I was sent here to watch you...

00:30:16.010 --> 00:30:18.205
to make sure
that you were all right.

00:30:18.246 --> 00:30:20.612
But now it's clear
that you are not.

00:30:20.648 --> 00:30:22.513
Who are you?

00:30:22.550 --> 00:30:24.984
We exist in what you would call

00:30:25.019 --> 00:30:28.921
a temporal inversion fold
in the space-time matrix.

00:30:28.956 --> 00:30:30.924
It's not necessary
to understand.

00:30:30.958 --> 00:30:33.756
It only matters
that there was an accident.

00:30:33.794 --> 00:30:36.991
Your shuttle intersected
one of our time-streams

00:30:37.098 --> 00:30:38.565
and... boom!

00:30:38.599 --> 00:30:42.000
A few things were altered
as the result of the accident.

00:30:42.103 --> 00:30:44.571
History and events
were scrambled a bit

00:30:44.605 --> 00:30:46.402
and you ended up here.

00:30:46.440 --> 00:30:48.965
Well, you've got to get me back.

00:30:49.010 --> 00:30:50.739
Ah...

00:30:50.778 --> 00:30:52.746
we don't know how.

00:30:52.780 --> 00:30:54.338
What?

00:30:54.382 --> 00:30:57.180
We only know
that an accident occurred.

00:30:57.218 --> 00:30:59.277
We don't know how or why.

00:30:59.320 --> 00:31:01.185
Well, that's not good enough.

00:31:01.222 --> 00:31:03.520
There's got to be
something we can do.

00:31:03.557 --> 00:31:05.525
Where is this time-stream
of yours?

00:31:05.559 --> 00:31:07.754
Maybe I can use it to get back.

00:31:07.795 --> 00:31:08.955
Mm...

00:31:08.996 --> 00:31:12.523
the time-stream weaves through
the galaxy like a thread.

00:31:12.566 --> 00:31:14.966
I could show you how to find it,
and you could try to recreate

00:31:15.036 --> 00:31:17.504
the conditions that existed
before the accident

00:31:17.538 --> 00:31:19.938
and fly back into it,
but there's no guarantee

00:31:19.974 --> 00:31:21.771
what will happen to you
if you do.

00:31:21.809 --> 00:31:22.833
What do you mean?

00:31:22.877 --> 00:31:25.903
Well, you may be able
to change reality again,

00:31:25.946 --> 00:31:29.473
but there's no way to predict
how it would change.

00:31:29.517 --> 00:31:32.486
You could end up at any point
in the space-time continuum.

00:31:32.520 --> 00:31:34.988
You might return
to your original reality,

00:31:35.056 --> 00:31:38.583
or you might find yourself
a billion years in the future,

00:31:38.626 --> 00:31:40.560
or at some time
before sentient life

00:31:40.594 --> 00:31:42.755
even existed on your planet.

00:31:42.797 --> 00:31:45.322
I guess I'll have
to take that chance

00:31:45.366 --> 00:31:49.302
because somehow
I have to get back.

00:31:50.538 --> 00:31:53.006
Are you so sure?

00:31:53.040 --> 00:31:55.235
This is a pretty good
place for you, Harry.

00:31:55.276 --> 00:31:57.301
You have a wonderful
job with Starfleet,

00:31:57.345 --> 00:31:59.336
a beautiful woman who loves you.

00:31:59.380 --> 00:32:03.146
Why be so quick
to turn your back on all this?

00:32:03.184 --> 00:32:06.153
Maybe this is your, uh... fate?

00:32:06.187 --> 00:32:08.087
Isn't that the word
your people use?

00:32:08.122 --> 00:32:09.953
That thing
which was meant to be?

00:32:09.990 --> 00:32:11.184
Hmm?

00:32:11.225 --> 00:32:14.717
Seems to me you're actually
a very lucky man.

00:32:18.065 --> 00:32:20.363
What about Danny Byrd?

00:32:20.401 --> 00:32:22.198
He isn't so lucky.

00:32:22.236 --> 00:32:24.864
And Tom Paris?

00:32:24.905 --> 00:32:28.705
Fate wasn't so kind to him.

00:32:28.743 --> 00:32:30.210
No.

00:32:30.244 --> 00:32:32.542
It isn't supposed
to be this way.

00:32:32.580 --> 00:32:36.414
I'm supposed to be on Voyager
in the Delta Quadrant,

00:32:36.450 --> 00:32:39.112
and that's where I have to go.

00:32:42.923 --> 00:32:44.914
Very well.

00:32:47.027 --> 00:32:49.495
This will tell you
where the time-stream

00:32:49.530 --> 00:32:51.555
intersects this region of space.

00:32:51.599 --> 00:32:54.193
That's as much
as I can do for you.

00:32:56.036 --> 00:32:57.128
Thanks.

00:32:59.940 --> 00:33:02.340
Good luck,
Harry Kim of Voyager.

00:33:02.376 --> 00:33:04.276
You're going to need it.

00:33:04.311 --> 00:33:06.506
Unless, of course,
you decide to stay.

00:33:06.547 --> 00:33:10.847
In which case, I'll see you
in the morning, same time...

00:33:10.885 --> 00:33:13.854
Vulcan mocha, extra sweet.

00:33:35.910 --> 00:33:36.877
Libby...

00:33:36.911 --> 00:33:38.879
I didn't hear you come in.

00:33:38.913 --> 00:33:39.880
Obviously.

00:33:39.914 --> 00:33:41.381
You're in enough trouble
as it is.

00:33:41.415 --> 00:33:43.975
What do you want them to do,
put you in prison?

00:33:44.051 --> 00:33:46.679
No...

00:33:46.720 --> 00:33:48.347
I'm just trying to get back
to where I belong.

00:33:48.389 --> 00:33:51.483
Where you belong.

00:33:51.525 --> 00:33:54.517
You used to say
you belonged here with me.

00:33:56.263 --> 00:33:58.197
But I guess everything's
changed, hasn't it?

00:33:58.232 --> 00:34:00.223
Look...

00:34:03.637 --> 00:34:04.797
I know the last few days

00:34:04.839 --> 00:34:06.101
must've been
pretty tough on you...

00:34:06.140 --> 00:34:07.300
Do you?!

00:34:07.341 --> 00:34:09.673
Do you really know
what it's like

00:34:09.710 --> 00:34:12.110
when the person you love
suddenly changes?

00:34:12.146 --> 00:34:14.808
It's still me... the guy who was

00:34:14.849 --> 00:34:18.444
in your seat
at the Ktarian music festival.

00:34:18.486 --> 00:34:20.681
The guy who took three weeks

00:34:20.721 --> 00:34:22.951
to work up the courage
to ask you out.

00:34:23.057 --> 00:34:26.686
The guy who still wakes up
in the middle of the night

00:34:26.727 --> 00:34:30.356
and says your name out loud,
hoping you'll answer back.

00:34:30.397 --> 00:34:32.888
But if you're really Harry,

00:34:32.933 --> 00:34:36.369
you wouldn't be trying so hard
to get away from me.

00:34:36.403 --> 00:34:38.598
I'm not trying
to get away from you.

00:34:38.639 --> 00:34:40.971
I love you.

00:34:41.075 --> 00:34:42.975
And I promise you

00:34:43.077 --> 00:34:46.478
I want to stay here
more than anything.

00:34:47.848 --> 00:34:50.146
But I can't.

00:34:50.184 --> 00:34:52.482
I don't understand.

00:34:52.520 --> 00:34:54.852
I don't understand any of this.

00:34:58.092 --> 00:35:01.994
I don't think anybody knows me
as well as you do.

00:35:03.397 --> 00:35:05.024
So you, of all people,
should know

00:35:05.065 --> 00:35:07.033
that once I've made up
my mind about something,

00:35:07.067 --> 00:35:09.058
I can't let it go.

00:35:11.205 --> 00:35:13.105
In some ways...

00:35:13.140 --> 00:35:15.506
it'd be a lot easier
to forget about Voyager,

00:35:15.543 --> 00:35:19.673
just settle in here
and build a life...

00:35:19.713 --> 00:35:22.841
but that wouldn't be me.

00:35:22.883 --> 00:35:24.851
You wouldn't be
getting the Harry Kim

00:35:24.885 --> 00:35:26.876
you fell in love with.

00:35:31.892 --> 00:35:33.860
Does that make any sense?

00:35:35.629 --> 00:35:37.256
The tampering alarm.

00:35:37.298 --> 00:35:39.357
Security will be here
any second.

00:35:39.400 --> 00:35:41.527
I better go.

00:35:41.569 --> 00:35:45.061
I promise you, I'm going
to try to get back.

00:35:45.105 --> 00:35:46.766
It may take awhile,

00:35:46.807 --> 00:35:52.006
and I may not make it,
but I swear I will try.

00:36:02.690 --> 00:36:04.681
Sorry.

00:36:29.216 --> 00:36:30.148
Hold it!

00:37:00.180 --> 00:37:01.442
Get up!

00:37:02.783 --> 00:37:03.772
Excuse me.

00:37:06.020 --> 00:37:07.851
There goes my bank shot.

00:37:07.888 --> 00:37:09.116
What are you doing here?

00:37:09.156 --> 00:37:10.919
Helping out a friend.

00:37:11.025 --> 00:37:13.016
Let's go.

00:37:21.666 --> 00:37:22.928
So how did you find me?

00:37:23.001 --> 00:37:24.696
I still have a few friends
at Starfleet.

00:37:24.736 --> 00:37:26.567
They told me you were
in some serious trouble.

00:37:26.605 --> 00:37:29.403
Yeah. Starfleet thinks
I'm a Maquis spy.

00:37:29.441 --> 00:37:30.669
I know the feeling.

00:37:30.709 --> 00:37:33.473
Those security anklets
really chafe, don't they?

00:37:33.511 --> 00:37:36.139
You're the last person
I expected to help me.

00:37:36.181 --> 00:37:38.115
Let's just say
it's been a long time

00:37:38.149 --> 00:37:41.880
since anybody gave a damn
about my future, including me.

00:37:41.920 --> 00:37:42.887
I don't know if I'm supposed

00:37:42.921 --> 00:37:44.889
to be on Voyager
like you've told me,

00:37:44.923 --> 00:37:47.483
but it sounds a whole lot better
than the life I have here.

00:37:47.525 --> 00:37:50.050
I'm willing to take
my chances, Ensign.

00:37:50.095 --> 00:37:51.687
Call me Harry.

00:37:51.730 --> 00:37:53.459
You always did.

00:37:53.498 --> 00:37:55.693
Won't be long
before they find us.

00:37:55.734 --> 00:37:57.258
We better keep moving.

00:37:57.302 --> 00:37:59.827
Wait, I found a way
to get back to my reality.

00:37:59.871 --> 00:38:01.532
The problem is
I'll need a ship to do it.

00:38:01.573 --> 00:38:03.541
I think I have access
to a runabout,

00:38:03.575 --> 00:38:06.009
but I'm going to have
to break it out of Spacedock.

00:38:06.044 --> 00:38:08.239
Sounds to me
like you need a pilot.

00:38:08.280 --> 00:38:10.145
Know anyone who's qualified?

00:38:10.181 --> 00:38:12.308
I know someone
who used to be pretty good,

00:38:12.350 --> 00:38:14.250
and if I'm not mistaken,
he still knows a few tricks.

00:38:14.286 --> 00:38:16.186
I have an office
at Starfleet Headquarters.

00:38:16.221 --> 00:38:17.188
I think we can access

00:38:17.222 --> 00:38:18.587
the runabout launch codes
from there.

00:38:18.623 --> 00:38:20.420
Site-to-site transporter.

00:38:20.458 --> 00:38:21.516
With friends like mine,

00:38:21.559 --> 00:38:23.390
you never know when
it'll come in handy.

00:38:23.428 --> 00:38:24.554
Where's your office?

00:38:24.596 --> 00:38:27.759
Main complex, Level 6,
Subsection 47.

00:38:27.799 --> 00:38:30.893
I can beam us in, but we'll
only have a few minutes

00:38:30.936 --> 00:38:32.927
before Security starts
kicking down the door.

00:38:33.004 --> 00:38:34.266
Let's do it.

00:38:40.578 --> 00:38:43.479
So, Harry, once we're
on board the runabout,

00:38:43.515 --> 00:38:44.709
what's the plan?

00:38:44.749 --> 00:38:46.046
The alien said
that if I recreate

00:38:46.084 --> 00:38:48.211
the conditions of the accident
and fly into the time-stream,

00:38:48.253 --> 00:38:50.778
there's a chance I might be able
to get back into my reality.

00:38:50.822 --> 00:38:52.187
Might?

00:38:52.223 --> 00:38:53.383
He couldn't give
me any guarantees.

00:38:54.759 --> 00:38:55.748
Security's just been alerted

00:38:55.794 --> 00:38:58.126
to an unauthorized transport
in the building.

00:38:58.163 --> 00:38:59.323
It'll take them
another 20 seconds

00:38:59.364 --> 00:39:00.331
to track it to this office.

00:39:00.365 --> 00:39:01.332
How are you coming?

00:39:01.366 --> 00:39:02.424
Almost there.

00:39:02.467 --> 00:39:05.300
I've bypassed the runabout
security lock-outs.

00:39:05.337 --> 00:39:06.531
They're onto us.

00:39:06.571 --> 00:39:07.663
We've got to go.

00:39:07.706 --> 00:39:08.934
Hold on.
I've almost got it.

00:39:09.841 --> 00:39:10.830
Now!

00:39:18.717 --> 00:39:20.548
Overriding initialization codes.

00:39:20.585 --> 00:39:22.416
Main power coming on line.

00:39:22.454 --> 00:39:24.581
Let's get those engines going.

00:39:24.622 --> 00:39:26.817
Powering up main fusion reactor.

00:39:26.858 --> 00:39:28.052
Intruder alert.

00:39:28.093 --> 00:39:30.561
Unauthorized launch in progress.

00:39:30.595 --> 00:39:32.893
The space door is closing.

00:39:32.931 --> 00:39:35.729
Warp core and main
propulsion are on line.

00:39:35.767 --> 00:39:38.497
Releasing docking clamps,
moorings cleared.

00:39:38.536 --> 00:39:40.128
Here we go.

00:39:48.013 --> 00:39:49.878
We're clear.

00:39:49.914 --> 00:39:51.609
I'm entering the coordinates

00:39:51.649 --> 00:39:54.243
of the time-stream
into the main computer.

00:39:54.285 --> 00:39:58.085
Adjusting course to match.
Going to full impulse.

00:39:58.123 --> 00:40:00.819
We've got a starship on
our tail... Nebula-class.

00:40:00.859 --> 00:40:02.724
I'll try to lose them, Harry,

00:40:02.761 --> 00:40:05.229
but they're a lot faster
than we are.

00:40:05.263 --> 00:40:07.390
Attention Runabout Yellowstone.

00:40:07.432 --> 00:40:10.367
Power down your engines
or we will open fire.

00:40:10.402 --> 00:40:11.369
They're going to try

00:40:11.403 --> 00:40:12.700
to do everything
they can to stop us.

00:40:12.737 --> 00:40:15.171
They think we're trying
to steal this prototype.

00:40:16.207 --> 00:40:18.232
They're closing
to 5,000 kilometers.

00:40:23.982 --> 00:40:25.813
Shields down to 70 percent!

00:40:26.918 --> 00:40:28.852
50 percent!

00:40:28.887 --> 00:40:30.184
29 percent!

00:40:30.221 --> 00:40:32.451
I thought you said this ship
was new and improved!

00:40:32.490 --> 00:40:33.923
It is.

00:40:33.958 --> 00:40:35.516
But it looks like they
haven't finished working

00:40:35.560 --> 00:40:36.584
on the defensive systems.

00:40:36.628 --> 00:40:38.186
In fact, some
of the safety interlocks

00:40:38.229 --> 00:40:39.253
aren't even in place.

00:40:39.297 --> 00:40:41.197
A few more of those hits
and I don't...

00:40:42.233 --> 00:40:43.996
We're losing
antimatter containment.

00:40:44.069 --> 00:40:45.832
Attempting
to stabilize the field.

00:40:45.870 --> 00:40:48.703
We're approaching the
coordinates of the time-stream.

00:40:50.708 --> 00:40:51.868
The containment field
is weakening.

00:40:51.910 --> 00:40:53.468
We could be looking
at a core breach.

00:40:53.511 --> 00:40:56.639
The ship's closing
to 3,000 kilometers.

00:40:56.681 --> 00:40:58.148
If we can't shake them off,

00:40:58.183 --> 00:40:59.810
maybe we can slow
them down a little.

00:40:59.851 --> 00:41:00.943
This runabout is equipped

00:41:00.985 --> 00:41:02.452
with tetryon plasma
warp nacelles.

00:41:02.487 --> 00:41:03.476
So?

00:41:03.521 --> 00:41:06.513
Tetryon plasma emits
multiflux gamma radiation.

00:41:06.558 --> 00:41:07.820
It disrupts subspace.

00:41:07.859 --> 00:41:09.554
We could vent the warp plasma.

00:41:09.594 --> 00:41:11.687
The second they hit
the plasma cloud,

00:41:11.729 --> 00:41:12.957
their engines would stall,

00:41:12.997 --> 00:41:14.487
give us a few seconds
of breathing room.

00:41:14.532 --> 00:41:15.692
Exactly.

00:41:15.733 --> 00:41:17.826
Unlocking the warp drive
manifold.

00:41:17.869 --> 00:41:19.971
Venting drive plasma.

00:41:25.743 --> 00:41:27.370
Any second...

00:41:29.680 --> 00:41:31.648
They've dropped
to one-tenth impulse.

00:41:34.752 --> 00:41:36.583
Our containment field's
at critical.

00:41:36.620 --> 00:41:37.644
We'd better hurry.

00:41:37.688 --> 00:41:40.418
All right, let's recreate
my shuttle accident.

00:41:40.458 --> 00:41:43.291
I think I was traveling
at 140,000 kph.

00:41:43.327 --> 00:41:44.487
You think?

00:41:44.528 --> 00:41:45.620
Look, that was another lifetime.

00:41:45.663 --> 00:41:47.096
I'm doing the best I can.

00:41:47.131 --> 00:41:50.828
Increasing speed to 140,000 kph.

00:41:50.868 --> 00:41:53.336
Now, I also remember
running a polaron scan.

00:41:53.371 --> 00:41:55.737
The scanning beam
was sweeping at a radius

00:41:55.773 --> 00:41:57.536
of half a million kilometers.

00:41:57.575 --> 00:41:59.566
No, wait...
a quarter million.

00:42:02.079 --> 00:42:04.479
Activating polaron scan.

00:42:04.515 --> 00:42:06.278
That should do it.

00:42:06.317 --> 00:42:07.682
Approaching coordinates.

00:42:07.718 --> 00:42:09.481
Impact in four...

00:42:09.520 --> 00:42:10.680
three...

00:42:10.721 --> 00:42:11.881
two...

00:42:14.525 --> 00:42:15.822
Did we miss it?

00:42:15.860 --> 00:42:17.828
We passed through
the coordinates,

00:42:17.862 --> 00:42:19.523
but the runabout was unaffected.

00:42:20.731 --> 00:42:22.358
The starship
has repowered its engines.

00:42:22.400 --> 00:42:24.334
They'll be here
in under a minute.

00:42:24.368 --> 00:42:26.598
I have to get
into that time-stream.

00:42:26.637 --> 00:42:27.968
Wait a minute.

00:42:28.005 --> 00:42:30.439
I'm forgetting something.

00:42:30.474 --> 00:42:31.805
The emergency transport.

00:42:31.842 --> 00:42:33.639
The last thing
I remember hearing

00:42:33.677 --> 00:42:35.474
was Captain Janeway's
com voice.

00:42:35.513 --> 00:42:37.845
She said she was trying
to beam me off the shuttle.

00:42:37.882 --> 00:42:40.146
That's it. I've got
to beam off the ship.

00:42:40.184 --> 00:42:41.515
Are you crazy?

00:42:41.552 --> 00:42:42.883
We have to recreate
all the conditions

00:42:42.920 --> 00:42:44.717
of the accident,
including that one.

00:42:44.755 --> 00:42:46.848
We just lost
antimatter containment.

00:42:46.891 --> 00:42:48.415
25 seconds to core breach.

00:42:48.459 --> 00:42:50.256
I've locked
onto the time-stream.

00:42:50.294 --> 00:42:51.886
Get on the transporter pad.

00:42:51.929 --> 00:42:53.157
Not yet.
The core's breaching.

00:42:53.197 --> 00:42:54.664
We've got to shut it down first.

00:42:54.698 --> 00:42:55.665
There's no time!

00:42:55.699 --> 00:42:57.189
That ship'll be here
in another 30 seconds!

00:42:57.234 --> 00:42:59.361
In 15 seconds, this ship
is going to explode.

00:42:59.403 --> 00:43:00.370
You'll be killed.

00:43:00.404 --> 00:43:02.031
Look! If you're right,
then things will be

00:43:02.073 --> 00:43:03.938
changed back to the way
they're supposed to be,

00:43:04.008 --> 00:43:05.635
and you'll find me
back on Voyager.

00:43:05.676 --> 00:43:07.610
And if I'm wrong,
if this doesn't work,

00:43:07.645 --> 00:43:09.169
you'll be blown up right here.

00:43:12.049 --> 00:43:13.380
Go!

00:43:18.456 --> 00:43:19.821
Voyager to Shuttlecraft Drake.

00:43:19.857 --> 00:43:22.257
Prepare for emergency transport.

00:43:22.293 --> 00:43:23.453
Mr. Kim, can you hear me?

00:43:23.494 --> 00:43:25.621
We're attempting
to lock onto you.

00:43:25.663 --> 00:43:26.789
Harry?

00:43:26.831 --> 00:43:27.957
Kim here, Captain.

00:43:27.998 --> 00:43:29.863
Harry, we need you
to drop your shields.

00:43:29.900 --> 00:43:32.095
Stand by.

00:43:32.136 --> 00:43:33.797
Shields down, Captain.

00:43:33.838 --> 00:43:35.169
Lieutenant.

00:43:35.206 --> 00:43:38.175
The anomaly is sending out
heavy subspace distortions.

00:43:38.209 --> 00:43:39.471
I can't get
a positive lock on him.

00:43:39.510 --> 00:43:41.239
The hull is starting
to buckle under the stress.

00:43:41.278 --> 00:43:42.802
He won't survive much longer.

00:43:42.847 --> 00:43:45.111
Tuvok, can you boost
the transporter signal?

00:43:45.149 --> 00:43:46.844
Negative. The signal
is at maximum gain.

00:43:46.884 --> 00:43:48.408
Ten seconds to hull breach.

00:43:48.452 --> 00:43:50.545
He's just out of reach.

00:43:50.588 --> 00:43:51.850
B'Elanna, can you
tie the transporter

00:43:51.889 --> 00:43:53.220
directly into the main
deflector dish.

00:43:53.257 --> 00:43:55.350
Use it to extend the signal.

00:43:55.392 --> 00:43:56.518
I'll try.

00:43:56.560 --> 00:43:57.959
Hull breach in progress.

00:44:00.131 --> 00:44:01.257
We've got him, Captain.

00:44:01.298 --> 00:44:03.664
Mr. Chakotay,
analyze the sensor logs.

00:44:03.701 --> 00:44:05.635
I want to know
what happened out there.

00:44:05.669 --> 00:44:06.829
Aye, Captain.

00:44:06.871 --> 00:44:08.805
Voyager to Transporter Room 2.

00:44:08.839 --> 00:44:10.329
Are you all right, Mr. Kim?

00:44:10.374 --> 00:44:11.636
I think so, Captain.

00:44:11.675 --> 00:44:13.142
Is Lieutenant Paris there?

00:44:13.177 --> 00:44:15.407
Yes, he's here.
Why?

00:44:15.446 --> 00:44:16.936
It's a long story.

00:44:16.981 --> 00:44:18.915
I look forward to hearing it.

00:44:18.949 --> 00:44:20.917
I'll be in my ready room.

00:44:26.457 --> 00:44:27.822
We think your shuttlecraft

00:44:27.858 --> 00:44:30.418
was caught in some kind
of temporal anomaly.

00:44:30.461 --> 00:44:31.553
A time-stream?

00:44:31.595 --> 00:44:33.358
Yes, you could call it that.

00:44:33.397 --> 00:44:36.059
I've already been briefed,
Commander.

00:44:36.100 --> 00:44:37.397
Welcome back.

00:44:37.434 --> 00:44:39.732
Kind of a rough ride, huh?

00:44:42.039 --> 00:44:43.870
What is it, Harry?

00:44:43.908 --> 00:44:45.899
I owe you one.
